---
import PortalLayout from '../layouts/PortalLayout.astro';
import { repository } from '../data/site';

const cloneCommand = 'git clone ' + repository + '.git\ncd alicorn';
---

<PortalLayout
  title="Build from source — Alicorn"
  description="Build Alicorn's native starter and explore the Odin GUI runtime from source."
  channel="BUILD"
>
  <section class="build-page page-section">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <p class="section-kicker">SOURCE-FIRST PROJECT</p>
      <h1>Build Alicorn.<br /><span>Then build your app.</span></h1>
      <p>
        Alicorn is a GUI runtime and library, not an end-user desktop application. Start from the
        repository, install the platform prerequisites, and run the native hello example.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="build-block">
      <div class="build-block-heading">
        <span>01</span>
        <div><h2>Get the source</h2><p>Clone the public repository and enter its root.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="command-box">
        <pre><code>git clone {repository}.git
cd alicorn</code></pre>
        <button type="button" data-copy={cloneCommand}>Copy</button>
      </div>
      <p class="build-note">
        The repository documents the Odin compiler version and native platform dependencies. Use
        the complete Odin distribution, including its <code>base</code>, <code>core</code>, and
        <code>vendor</code> directories.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/docs/getting-started/requirements">Check prerequisites <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </section>

    <section class="build-block">
      <div class="build-block-heading">
        <span>02</span>
        <div><h2>Run the native starter</h2><p>Choose the script for your shell.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="command-grid">
        <div class="command-card">
          <span class="command-label">macOS / Linux</span>
          <div class="command-box">
            <pre><code>./tools/native_hello.sh</code></pre>
            <button type="button" data-copy="./tools/native_hello.sh">Copy</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="command-card">
          <span class="command-label">Windows PowerShell</span>
          <div class="command-box">
            <pre><code>.\tools\native_hello.ps1</code></pre>
            <button type="button" data-copy=".\\tools\\native_hello.ps1">Copy</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="build-note">
        The starter rebuilds before launch. Its source is <code>examples/01_hello/main.odin</code>;
        the <a href="/docs/getting-started/first-app">first app guide</a> shows how to change it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="build-block build-block--dark">
      <div class="build-block-heading">
        <span>03</span>
        <div><h2>Build a native package</h2><p>Packaging tools are for Alicorn applications you create.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p>
        The repository includes Windows and macOS helpers for producing an unsigned application
        package with the SDL host. Your application still owns its display name, icon, signing,
        notarization, installer, and update policy.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href={repository + '/blob/master/docs/packaging.md'}>Read native packaging <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </section>

    <p class="build-footnote">
      There are no Alicorn binary installers on this page. Use the repository's current
      <a href={repository + '/releases'}>release page</a> for any published artifacts.
    </p>
  </section>
</PortalLayout>
